# Deploy + GitHub Push

Whenever you run a build and deploy (`npm run build && firebase deploy --only hosting`), you must also commit any uncommitted changes and push to GitHub immediately after.

## Steps after every deploy

1. `git add -A` — stage all changes
2. `git commit -m "..."` — write a concise commit message summarising what was deployed
3. `git push` — push to the remote branch

Do this automatically without waiting to be asked, as part of every deploy workflow.
